  "blocks": {
    "\"Check AGENTS.md — someone pasted the entire style guide in there instead of putting it behind a skill.\"": "“检查 AGENTS.md——有人把整份样式指南粘了进去，而不是放在技能后面按需加载。”",
    "\"Why is every session starting with 4k tokens already burned?\"": "“为什么每次会话刚开始就已经消耗了 4k Token？”",
    "A file in the environment that the harness loads into the context window at session start — the project's standing brief to the agent. Cross-harness convention; some harnesses also have their own variant (Claude Code's is CLAUDE.md).": "AGENTS.md 是位于<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/environment\">环境</a>中的文件，由<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/harness\">运行框架</a>在<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>开始时加载进<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-window\">上下文窗口</a>；它相当于项目长期提供给<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>的工作简报。这是一项跨运行框架约定，某些框架也有自己的变体，例如 Claude Code 使用 <code>CLAUDE.md</code>。",
    "Avoid: using AGENTS.md for content that should be progressively disclosed — anything in it pays a token cost every turn, in every session, whether or not that session needs it. A style guide can go behind a skill or a context pointer instead; keep AGENTS.md for the lines that apply everywhere.": "<em>避免：</em>把本应<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/progressive-disclosure\">渐进式披露</a>的内容写进 AGENTS.md。无论会话是否需要，其中每项内容都会在每个会话的每个<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/turn\">轮次</a>支付 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/token\">Token</a> 成本。样式指南可以放在<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/skill\">技能</a>或<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-pointer\">上下文指针</a>之后；AGENTS.md 只保留适用于所有场景的规则。",
    "Because it loads automatically, it's one way to avoid repeating yourself across sessions. The model is stateless — a correction you give in one session is gone in the next, and you end up telling every fresh session that the project uses pnpm, that tests run with a particular flag, that a directory is generated and shouldn't be touched. When you've corrected the agent for the same thing twice, that correction is a candidate line for AGENTS.md.": "因为它会自动加载，所以可以帮助你避免在不同会话中反复解释。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/model\">模型</a>是<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/stateless\">无状态</a>的——一次会话中的纠正不会保留到下一次，于是你不得不告诉每个新会话：项目使用 pnpm、测试必须带某个选项运行、某个目录由工具生成不得修改。当你已经针对同一件事纠正智能体两次，这条纠正就适合写进 AGENTS.md。",
    "Suitable content is whatever the agent can't derive from the code: build and test commands, conventions the codebase doesn't make obvious, hard constraints (\"never edit the generated client\"). Short and declarative — it's a brief, not documentation.": "适合写入的内容，是智能体无法直接从代码推导出的信息：构建和测试命令、代码库中不明显的约定，以及“绝不修改生成的客户端”这类硬性约束。内容应简短、直接陈述——它是一份简报，不是完整文档。",
    "The trade-off is that everything in it is always loaded. Instructions accumulate, most of them irrelevant to any given task, and a long AGENTS.md both costs tokens and dilutes itself — the more instructions in context, the less reliably the model follows any one of them.": "代价是其中所有内容都会始终加载。指令不断累积，而大部分对任一具体任务都无关；过长的 AGENTS.md 既消耗 Token，也会稀释自身效果——上下文中的指令越多，模型可靠遵循其中任意一条的概率就越低。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
  },
